  "verbalization": "Isocarboxazid is linked to Anxiety Disorder through a series of pharmacological pathways that involve endogenous depression. The evidence suggests that Isocarboxazid may act as a mediator in the development of anxiety by influencing the endogenous depression pathway, which is associated with multiple antidepressant agents. This connection is supported by the shared indication of Endogenous Depression in all three paths, which in turn are linked to Anxiety Disorder. The presence of multiple agents—Trazodone, Levomilnacipran, and Gepirone—suggesting a broader role in the pathophysiology of anxiety, reinforces the hypothesis that Isocarboxazid may contribute to the pathogenesis of anxiety through its interaction with these antidepressant pathways. The integrated evidence highlights a potential mechanism where Isocarboxazid influences the endogenous depression system, which is a key component in the treatment of anxiety disorders.",
